'' RUN: a bitfield that does not fit the open run starts a NEW run of its own type. 'd : 10
'' as ushort' after two ubyte bitfields went into an 8-bit unit (5 bytes, d = 1023 read 255);
'' a union bitfield reserves its whole unit. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/bitfield-overflow.bas -o tests/codegen/bitfieldoverflow.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/bitfieldoverflow.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  12            7             15            1023          1048575       12345678
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  8             4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4            127           3             -1            32767         -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: neg1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  0             0
